<xml xmlns="https://developers.google.com/blockly/xml"><variables><variable id="RHS}akw79O$=ZVwMF$]_">name</variable><variable id="Z9s!7o=4?O)sX#[1Ms,C">numStudents</variable><variable id="!ihY]nAys!JOOhpy[qih">numHungryStudents</variable><variable id="|lPr){^{Af-xhv^,QHLr">playerAnswer</variable></variables><block type="function_definition" id="XbD*fNs$2m6C-s22pNg0" x="1117" y="-207"><mutation name="getAndDisplayPlayerName" functionid="f/yMxBA,mM}a2#,T1Y}8"></mutation><field name="function_name">getAndDisplayPlayerName</field><comment pinned="true" h="402" w="370">This code uses the "settings" extension to permanently store the players's name.

An if block checks to see if the setting already exists:

- IF it does, it retrieves the value from settings

- ELSE it asks the player to enter their name

After the IF block, a simple Hello message is displayed which combines text with the "name" variable.</comment><data>{"commentRefs":[],"fieldData":{"~commentOffsetX":"-409.55555555555554","~commentOffsetY":"-22.888888888888886"}}</data><statement name="STACK"><block type="controls_if" id="Cp-76,,0H`mD=3PLJzj4"><mutation else="1"></mutation><value name="IF0"><shadow type="logic_boolean" id="p;-4NrO8lA?02q^bQO5$"><field name="BOOL">TRUE</field></shadow><block type="block_settings_exists" id="`;Wns+?#T^g3eD/JCx{d"><value name="name"><shadow type="text" id="qgmpZ^kRToe}=FH[1LFB"><field name="TEXT">name</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="variables_set" id="=fJEoT}V|2`eQq8+Q~X}"><field name="VAR" id="RHS}akw79O$=ZVwMF$]_">name</field><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="|j*1{LD4DquZ0+50JT%r"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow><block type="block_settings_read_string" id="^uF$ril8CA,5aUC+G?9B"><value name="name"><shadow type="text" id="l8YRU1+QcllK1U)@z$zj"><field name="TEXT">name</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></statement><statement name="ELSE"><block type="variables_set" id="Hg28l_:/4)2E`uR.$Ky{"><field name="VAR" id="RHS}akw79O$=ZVwMF$]_">name</field><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="m3b)3*ZVCDDmzH({%X6y"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow><block type="gameaskforstring" id="CTo0995N|MFB!tzq([E7"><mutation xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" _expanded="0" _input_init="true"></mutation><value name="message"><shadow type="text" id="B4SR]+D5SJ)VQJ^%6RqQ"><field name="TEXT">What is your name?</field></shadow></value><value name="answerLength"><shadow type="math_number_minmax" id="EE23,7hfGm$6fuY]Vo8t"><mutation min="1" max="24" label="AnswerLength" precision="0"></mutation><field name="SLIDER">12</field></shadow></value><value name="useOnScreenKeyboard"><shadow type="logic_boolean" id="dFm]f%F69s:*Y{4k9|a|"><field name="BOOL">FALSE</field></shadow></value></block></value><next><block type="block_settings_write_string" id=".(a|ZKqoShWUREerj/Zg"><value name="name"><shadow type="text" id="60j1#Sl`f8?+GJ@jc;g6"><field name="TEXT">name</field></shadow></value><value name="value"><shadow type="text" id="bP{+RZ]}|RM5Yfc]dv*F"><field name="TEXT"></field></shadow><block type="variables_get" id="QeUO73er=I-dY|4ejF;l"><field name="VAR" id="RHS}akw79O$=ZVwMF$]_">name</field></block></value></block></next></block></statement><next><block type="gameSplash" id="4%F^4=aj,Tg{oJ(iVChk"><mutation xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" _expanded="0" _input_init="true"></mutation><value name="title"><shadow type="text" id="U-{33!v5Vu-1UhlBOO1["><field name="TEXT"></field></shadow><block type="text_join" id="g^CDjVHZdK|^=M@OTI7B"><mutation items="3"></mutation><value name="ADD0"><shadow type="text" id="/PlSA`ln@Nzr]EwEv1Be"><field name="TEXT">Hello, </field></shadow></value><value name="ADD1"><shadow type="text" id="Rr!kL$zJ:$@^O~Q6%.)s"><field name="TEXT">World</field></shadow><block type="variables_get" id="o~v%^Tg2~wmiEdb9pV2a"><field name="VAR" id="RHS}akw79O$=ZVwMF$]_">name</field></block></value><value name="ADD2"><shadow type="text" id="*YzB]/FWA+rpwi4$jMoX"><field name="TEXT">!</field></shadow></value></block></value><value name="subtitle"><shadow type="text" id="htNV/*/5.)l+On9kcAwp"><field name="TEXT"></field></shadow></value></block></next></block></statement></block><block type="pxt-on-start" id="ZM,,0zLyM0ckRtSAG=Wv" x="-2040" y="-17"><comment pinned="true" h="583" w="370">This code uses the code for the previous tutorials, placing the code neatly in functions:
- getAndDisplayPlayerName
- welcomeToOzHarvest
- calculateNumberOfHungryStudents

To make this easier to test, you can simply drag the function blocks outside the start block to test other code on its own.

Now it's your turn to create your own learning activity. Remember that we have learnt how to:
- Ask for a player's name and store it in a setting (the program remembers it for next time)
- Used the story extension with player choices to enable the player to select a correct answer
- Ask for a number and use maths blocks to calculate a correct maths answer
- Used images and long text to explore narrative themes of food waste and hunger</comment><data>{"commentRefs":[],"fieldData":{"~commentOffsetX":"-422.8888888888889","~commentOffsetY":"-10.666666666666664"}}</data><statement name="HANDLER"><block type="function_call" id="W^RM3g=znmS@2^0t%Hrd"><mutation name="getAndDisplayPlayerName" functionid="f/yMxBA,mM}a2#,T1Y}8"></mutation><next><block type="function_call" id=";2xl)+OG4(8F$v^#hV?;"><mutation name="WelcomeToOzHarvest" functionid="|^@3!]3i{7!em?)KQ]VO"></mutation><next><block type="function_call" id="*+i/o)Kj?}Af;~?hif!@"><mutation name="calculateNumberOfHungryStudents" functionid="HT_BJM5W,K}eGae4^hU^"></mutation></block></next></block></next></block></statement></block><block type="function_definition" id="Z+:w_1uVPbcsNc(FgI_;" x="-1217" y="-50"><mutation name="calculateNumberOfHungryStudents" functionid="HT_BJM5W,K}eGae4^hU^"></mutation><field name="function_name">calculateNumberOfHungryStudents</field><comment pinned="true" h="555" w="406">This next part of the game uses "ask for number" (instead of "ask for string"), to get the player to input a number instead.

After getting the number of students in the class, the program also asks for the number of hungry students in the class
(1 in 9)

Then the program calculates the number of hungry students by using maths blocks (floor and /)

Finally the program checks if the answer is correct, and displays a correct or incorret message.</comment><data>{"commentRefs":[],"fieldData":{"~commentOffsetX":"-435.1111111111111","~commentOffsetY":"-15.11111111111111"}}</data><statement name="STACK"><block type="gamesetbackgroundimage" id="nHvicfaSCe}BFl5~R][#"><value name="img"><shadow type="background_image_picker" id=";fc%o%,iGsCJummv]}d8"><field name="img">img`
